@startuml ray-scan
' SPEC: _spec/packages/starchess-core/ray-scan.puml
' purpose: board/ray-scan.ts — walk a ray once, classify the first thing met.
' Authority: this is shipped.
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess Core · ""scanRay"" — one walk, one contact

start
:""mids = rayBetween(from, intentTo)"";
repeat :next intermediate ""at"";
  if (occupied?) then (no)
    :keep walking;
  else (yes)
    :""startVisible = canSee(color, at)"";
    :""revealSteps = pathRevealSteps(from → intentTo, at)"";
    :""becomesVisible = !startVisible && revealSteps > 0"";
    :""discovery"" = the intermediate that first lights ""at"";
    :""stopBefore"" = the last empty square before ""at"";
    :**return this contact** — nothing past it can matter;
    stop
  endif
repeat while (more intermediates?) is (yes)
->no;
:no contact — the ray is clear;
note right
  **What it replaced.** ""resolveTurn"" walked a ray in two places with
  near-identical ~90-line bodies (mid-path unit beats a further target; generic
  slide into fog), each re-deciding ally / king / fogged / lit / discovery in
  its own order. Both now call ""scanRay"" and keep only their distinct tail:
  * **targeted intent** — ally ⇒ quiet truncate · king ⇒ fall through to the
    generic walk · enemy ⇒ ""takeRayContact"";
  * **generic slide** — ally ⇒ quiet · king ⇒ fog ccShot or stop short ·
    enemy ⇒ ""takeRayContact"".

  ""takeRayContact"" is the shared classification the two loops used to spell out
  twice: still fogged ⇒ ""moveCollisions"" + occupy (sieged rooks fizzle) ·
  lights mid-walk ⇒ phase-3 approach · visible ⇒ phase-1 attack + occupy.

  **Still open:** ""scanRay"" calls ""pathRevealSteps"" once per contact, and that
  helper still rebuilds the placement map and full side vision for every
  intermediate it tests. A ""litAtStep"" map computed in the same single walk
  would answer every target on the ray for one pass.
end note
stop
@enduml
